Package: oneplus-erhai-cam
Version: 1.3
Section: oldlibs
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: TheMojoMan <themojoman@gmx.net>
Depends: oneplus-erhai-erhaicam (>= 1.4)
Description: transitional package — ErhaiCam was renamed to oneplus-erhai-erhaicam
 The ErhaiCam GTK4/GStreamer camera app used to be packaged as
 oneplus-erhai-cam (<= 1.2).  It is now oneplus-erhai-erhaicam, which ships the
 same application (the binary is still /usr/bin/erhai-cam) and declares
 Provides/Replaces/Breaks on the old name.
 .
 This package is EMPTY on purpose: it exists so that a device which still has
 oneplus-erhai-cam installed upgrades through apt instead of keeping a retired
 package forever.  Installing it pulls oneplus-erhai-erhaicam, and the file
 hand-over (usr/bin/erhai-cam, usr/share/applications/…, the shipped source)
 is done by that package's Replaces/Breaks on oneplus-erhai-cam (<< 1.3).
 .
 It is safe to remove once nothing depends on it:
     sudo apt purge oneplus-erhai-cam
